1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,750
What if my skin dermatitis worsens?

2
00:00:03,375 --> 00:00:07,041
Part Two: Silver Cream and Mepilex Padding

3
00:00:08,250 --> 00:00:12,166
90% of patients get through the first step of
 skin care management 

4
00:00:12,166 --> 00:00:13,791
and don't have further damage.

5
00:00:13,958 --> 00:00:16,833
But for about 10 to 15% of our patients,

6
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:20,333
  they will experience a higher grade of 
radiation dermatitis.

7
00:00:20,791 --> 00:00:24,208
Patients with this degree of skin dermatitis experience

8
00:00:24,208 --> 00:00:28,291
moist desquamation or opening of the skin.

9
00:00:28,291 --> 00:00:31,166
These using breaks in the skin pose two issues:

10
00:00:31,541 --> 00:00:35,083
1) greater pain and 2) a higher risk for infection.

11
00:00:35,083 --> 00:00:37,375
To treat this higher grade skin damage,

12
00:00:37,375 --> 00:00:42,500
we use astronger cream, Silver Sulfadiazene 
or Silvadene.

13
00:00:42,875 --> 00:00:45,583
This cream offers greater protection to the skin

14
00:00:45,583 --> 00:00:49,125
and an antibiotic component to prevent infection.

15
00:00:50,208 --> 00:00:53,750
To use this silver cream, apply it twice a day,

16
00:00:53,750 --> 00:00:56,208
once in the morning and once at night

17
00:00:56,208 --> 00:00:59,916
to all the areas of the skin
that are now open and oozing.

18
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:04,500
You have the option to use this
silver cream with this spot method: 

19
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:09,375
only covering up the open areas of skin
in conjunction with moisturizer,

20
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:12,833
which is still applied
to all other areas of the head and neck.

21
00:01:13,916 --> 00:01:16,791
Or you can simply apply the silver cream,

22
00:01:16,791 --> 00:01:20,166
like moisturizer, everywhere on the head and neck.

23
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:24,458
This silver cream is not over-the-counter

24
00:01:24,458 --> 00:01:26,958
and is available only via prescription.

25
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:30,666
Please check in with your doctor
and their team for a script.

26
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:33,000
Samples are also available.

27
00:01:34,166 --> 00:01:36,000
In addition to the silver cream, 

28
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,083
we have padding to further protect those 
areas of greater skin damage,

29
00:01:40,083 --> 00:01:43,750
high friction and or higher sensitivity to touch, 

30
00:01:43,750 --> 00:01:48,125
such as the skin near the shirt collar, 
backpack straps, etc.

31
00:01:48,583 --> 00:01:52,041
This padding is administered after 
applying the silver cream

32
00:01:52,041 --> 00:01:55,333
and can be cut to fit hard to reach areas.

33
00:01:55,958 --> 00:01:57,208
Like a band aid,

34
00:01:57,208 --> 00:01:59,875
Mepilex padding has adhesive edges

35
00:01:59,875 --> 00:02:03,750
with a soft center
and come in a variety of different sizes.

36
00:02:03,916 --> 00:02:06,666
We will provide you with these Mepilex Paddings.

37
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:11,666
Please do not place the adhesive
edges over open oozing areas.

38
00:02:12,250 --> 00:02:13,625
A note on dress:

39
00:02:14,125 --> 00:02:17,625
To further reduce discomfort,
we ask if you can wear low

40
00:02:17,625 --> 00:02:20,916
neck shirts that decrease the potential
for friction rubs.

41
00:02:20,916 --> 00:02:21,708
Of course,

42
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:26,375
this is not always possible due to dress
requirements for work and daily life.
